Reproducible cargo_build_script C/C++ objects.

cc-rs passes absolute source paths under the per-action exec root (which, in the
persistent-container strategy, contains a per-action sandbox number). The cc toolchain's
-ffile-prefix-map=/proc/self/cwd=. does not match those, so the sandbox path leaked into
DW_AT_comp_dir/DW_AT_name and every build-script-compiled object differed between builds.
Append -ffile-prefix-map=${pwd}=. (the runner substitutes ${pwd} with the exec root).

--- cargo/private/cargo_build_script.bzl
+++ cargo/private/cargo_build_script.bzl
@@ -502,6 +502,14 @@
         # for example, itself derived from the `macos_minimum_os` Bazel argument).
         env["CFLAGS"] = " ".join(_pwd_flags(cc_c_args))
         env["CXXFLAGS"] = " ".join(_pwd_flags(cc_cxx_args))
+
+        # cc-rs compiles with absolute paths under the (per-action) exec root, which the
+        # toolchain's /proc/self/cwd prefix map does not cover. Map the exec root to "." so
+        # build-script-compiled objects are reproducible.
+        if not cc_toolchain.compiler.startswith("msvc"):
+            prefix_map = "-ffile-prefix-map=${pwd}=."
+            env["CFLAGS"] = " ".join([env["CFLAGS"], prefix_map]).strip()
+            env["CXXFLAGS"] = " ".join([env["CXXFLAGS"], prefix_map]).strip()
         # It may be tempting to forward ARFLAGS, but cc-rs is opinionated enough
         # that doing so is more likely to hurt than help. If you need to change
         # ARFLAGS, make changes to cc-rs.
